# Copy this file to .dev.vars for local development. `wrangler dev` loads
# .dev.vars automatically, and `pnpm register` reads it via --env-file.
#
# In production the bot token is a secret:
#   wrangler secret put DISCORD_TOKEN
# DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY and DISCORD_CLIENT_ID are not sensitive, so they can go in
# the `vars` block of wrangler.jsonc instead, or be set as secrets as well.

# Bot token from the Discord developer portal (Bot -> Token).
# DISCORD_TOKEN=

# Public key used to verify incoming interaction signatures
# (General Information -> Public Key).
# DISCORD_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Application ID of the Discord app (General Information -> Application ID).
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
